{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484933-non-canon-uabrm-survivors","id":1484933,"title":"Non-canon UABRM Survivors","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-06-24T20:55:41-07:00","id":1484933,"title":"Non-canon UABRM Survivors","content":"Chicago has had the most By Night books so far with each one adding more and more interesting characters (my favorites from Onyx Path's being Malenkov, Sun Che and Flyboy), and while a lot of 1E characters were killed off in the WTA crossover book, v5 brought a few back. Tamoszius &quot;Nero&quot; is the sort of zany aloof artist who makes for a great decoration piece in basically any scene he ends up in and Levesque's feud with Balthazar is compelling plot that would've been wasted if not for his return. Both made me look into what other opportunities for good storytelling were lost after <i>Under a Blood Red Moon</i> released and makes me consider resurrecting more for my own game.<br /> <br /> The following characters are some that might have interesting reactions to how the world has progressed into the digital era or have unfulfilled/new plots with the other Chicago Kindred, many of whom have changed since the time of the werewolf attack. All of the following is just speculation as to how these characters would look if I were to try bringing them back<br /> <br /> <b>-Hank Cave</b>: Giving a brilliant and conceited beatnik the internet would be like leading a duck to water and he'd very likely accrue great acclaim for his dreary poetry if its even a tiny bit good, but his identity can essentially be boiled down to &quot;snazzy counterculture cat&quot;, counterculture ironically becoming more mainstream today. Would he lean into his former interests now that he might finally receive the recognition his genius always deserved, or would the many hipsters giving him dirty looks for smoking his cigarettes indoors give him pause? Theres no shortage of social movements he could throw his weight behind like the old days but few have the genuine passion the Black Panthers had, would he be discouraged that maybe &quot;the man&quot; has won? Would he shrug and remark that at least its easier to find blood laced with reefer these days, assured that no matter how many posers there are out there, he'd always fight the good fight? All of this would be secondary to his beef with Lodin should he discover the old roach is still around, of course. Does he still have a coffee shop with an exhausted boomer ghoul that grumbles about no one wanting to work anymore? Sell out to the Hellenes and make a fortune off his pretentiousness, or remain with Maldavis until she dies or runs off to join House Carna<br /> <br /> -<b>Travis Fett:</b> A Brujah with a grudge against the man who killed his sire, which is remarkably different from the Brujah with a grudge against the man who killed his grandsire, fyi. His search for the black childe of Lodin dressed like a Blood would end when he wakes up to find a black Childe of Lodin with ties to the Bloods occupying the city's throne, placing Travis firmly in the Anarch camp until he's dealt with. That's basically guaranteed. But whereas Marc Levesque is a follower of Anita Wainwright, Travis seems more macho, wanting to be the type of vato he never could be in real life, while not exactly coming across as a genuine rebel. Would he be attracted to Gengis' side of saber rattling while still enjoying the finer things in life, seeking to take down Prince Jackson while also claiming a spot on that List of 10? As for his hobbies he's a great entertainer with plenty of talents, perhaps he mentors young comedians similar to how Bret Styker does with aspiring dancers if he doesn't pursue the spotlight himself<br /> <br /> <b>-Priscilla Gibbs: </b>Setting aside how great of an antagonist Gordon Keaton would be in the modern society that worships slick soulless yuppies, the Madame could be one of the most well-connected vampires in Chicago with her escort service, especially if she hasn't been in torpor like the other returning characters. A black book of names filled with politicians, businessmen, who knows who else built up since the 90's and no blood bond to Keaton to keep her under his thumb could have the other Kindred almost overlooking her clanless status, especially if she diversifies her erotic portfolio. Does she seek a place in the Cam as she's hardly phased by the discrimination she'd face, money and power over everything, or is it more fulfilling to associate with the Anarchs and Erzulie's Blood Disco? Maybe she has too much dirt on influential mortals for the SI to ignore and she gets caught in her own web before V5 ever takes place. One more pretty schemer for thirsty players to offer their services and dignity to, add it to the pile<br /> <br /> <b>-Elzbieta Jurofsky:</b> Khalid's greatest admirer and Annabelle's self-appointed rival, Elzbieta would have plenty to do had she survived. Who else would see through Calhoun's impersonation of the Primogen faster, and take greater offense to the crime, than she would? She's also the only other vampire Nate Bordruff could tolerate at the time, and while she certainly doesn't share the sentiment, nothing would stop her from unleashing that hound if she had the chance. Knowing Khalid is really gone might lead to an investigation that likely leads to a certain tattooed lady and the Bahari, all of which would probably end up as her doing the introductory legwork on the Nerissa Blackwater plotline if the players haven't cared about it for a while. Would she take the position of Primogen if Cedrick gets caught? Disappear along with her sire?<br /> <br /> <b>-Sophia Ayes:</b> Probably Bret's only real friend, she would likely still be trying to perfect her &quot;art&quot; and finally appease her sire, but its her potential interactions with Helena that are really interesting. She could certainly join her broodmate in keeping their elder fed with new embraces, or while away the nights completely unaware of the atrocities he's become quite comfortable committing, but what happens if she ends up on the wrong side of those fangs? If she's killed and Bret finds out about it, would he even care enough to mention it to his new mistress? Maybe that is what it takes for the unapologetic heel to finally get his WWE face-turn, exposing the methuselah once and for all as he resolves to never be her pawn again (before he inevitably goes crawling back to Annabelle). If she doesn't end up dying tragically, well, you can never have too many Harpies in the Elysium, right?<br /> <br /> <b>-Pham Hong</b>: Among the most competent of the Chicago Ventrue, if he isn't the one to take the Princedom after Joseph Peterson has his Olympics fiasco, he'd make for a great handler for Camarilla characters along with Wauneka while also feuding with the guy for trying to restrict his access to Vietnam-vet blood, maybe settling for Gulf-War vets while complaining about the taste differences from the prescription painkillers so many seem hooked on. Whereas Horatio Ballard's stock deteriorated since the 90's, Pham's prospects can only improve once Lodin's no longer on top, especially when Capone goes missing and the organized crime market opens up. Both he and Jackson were their sire's childe embraced from ethnic minority backgrounds so perhaps the two would sympathize and respect one another, or perhaps they view each other as their primary competition<br /> <br /> <b>-Edgar Drummond:</b> Fuck cars, I want more chugga chugga Ventrue choo trains. How many hundreds of miles has the Loop expanded to cover Chicago now that no one's keeping an eye on Prince Drummond, Lord of the Rail?<br /> <br /> Have thoughts on how any of these characters would do if they appeared in V5's Chicago by Night? Another character I didn't mention or who is not from Chicago by Night who you'd consider worth reviving? Already brought back one of your favorites and want to share how things went down? Would love to hear it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27386,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27386-westfellow","user":"Westfellow","date":".  capone was pham's sire, not lodin 06-25-2022, 01:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27386-westfellow","name":"Westfellow","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-24T22:57:27-07:00","id":1484943,"title":"","content":"The original Chicago By Night had a lot of great characters, so it is no surprise that the large number of casualties in UBRM eliminated characters I would have preferred to keep. It'd be easier to list the characters that were killed that would not really be missed.<br /> <br /> All of the characters from the Jungle were great, and that's no surprise because it is a great work of literature. Those characters had a depth that many other characters did not.<br /> <br /> I liked Horace Turnbull. He was a great ancilla. He sided with the elders, but could help neonate PCs navigate vampire society.<br /> <br /> I also liked Lawrence Ballard. There is a tendency of some Ventrue to embrace within their own mortal lineage, and the link between Horatio and Lawrence Ballard was one of the few canonical examples we had of that. I would have liked to see some Ballard Ventrues in Chicago as either Horatio or Lawrence saw someone with potential so we could have this little dynasty.<br /> <br /> And Gordon Keaton was such a great bastard, that eliminating him removed someone who would have been a great villain in any chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-24T23:33:24-07:00","id":1484946,"title":"","content":"Another new Ballard would have been quite welcome, especially if it was one of the kids he'd make serve him for a week who finally grew up and knows far too many of his secrets. Or if they didn't want to leave the Hecata's offer to make the Ballards another minor family to the storytellers choice they could have one of his family show up as the Hecata's secretly embraced representative and he flips his lid. Keaton being Francois Mamuwalde's sire is the sort of sadistic irony that makes him great, he'd really fit in with the nihilists when he's not harassing the blood disco or canoodling with Balthazar. Gotta have him in there","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27386-westfellow","name":"Westfellow","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-25T01:51:16-07:00","id":1484951,"title":"","content":"I am currently STing Chicago by Night 1st edition. At the conclusion of Anabelle's Party (form Succubus Club sourcebook) Drummond was exiled from Chicago because of the players's action. If we ever run UABRM (I have it in the reserve, pending players ' future actions) they would have actually saved Drummond's life and he could be back.<br /> As I side note, I tuned down Drummond's comic relief tone and I made him into a sad, old fashioned relic from the past, which worked really well","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}